  "A:Slide 9 of 9: Saskatoon": "Pichait 9 eng' 9: Saskatoon",
  "Canada's largest city, home to the 553-metre CN Tower, the world's tallest free-standing structure for more than 30 years.": "Taunit ne oo missing eng' Kanada, ole mi CN Tower ne koi mita 553, kaa ne ki koi missing eng' ng'wony eng' kenyisiek kosiir 30.",
  "Regularly ranked among the world's most liveable cities, set between the Pacific Ocean and the Coast Mountains.": "Kegeer kasarta ak kasarta kou agenge eng' taunisiek che kararan missing eng' sobet eng' ng'wony, ne mi kwenutab Pacific Ocean ak Coast Mountains.",
  "One of the world's largest French-speaking cities, built around Mount Royal, the hill it takes its name from.": "Agenge eng' taunisiek che echen missing eng' ng'wony che ng'alalei Kifaransa, ne kichob kogole Mount Royal, tulwet ne kigoon kainet.",
  "Canada's capital, home to Parliament Hill and a Rideau Canal that becomes the world's largest naturally frozen skating rink each winter.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab Kanada, ole mi Parliament Hill ak Rideau Canal ne walaksei koek ole ne oo missing eng' ng'wony ne kiwendoi eng' barafu eng' kasarta ab kaitit age tugul.",
  "Host of the 1988 Winter Olympics and the annual Calgary Stampede, with the Canadian Rockies close by.": "Ki kiyai eng' yu Winter Olympics ab 1988, ak kiyaei Calgary Stampede kenyit age tugul; ak Canadian Rockies ko mi negit.",
  "Alberta's capital, known as the \"Festival City\" and home to West Edmonton Mall, the largest shopping mall in North America.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab Alberta, ne kigure \"Festival City\", ole mi West Edmonton Mall, duka ne oo missing eng' North America.",
  "The capital of Manitoba, built where the Red and Assiniboine rivers meet at The Forks, a gathering place for thousands of years and now home to the Canadian Museum for Human Rights.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab Manitoba, ne kichob ole tuiyei oinosiek ab Red ak Assiniboine eng' The Forks, ole ne ki tuiyei biik eng' kenyisiek eliphuusyek, ak raini ko mi Canadian Museum for Human Rights.",
  "Nova Scotia's capital and the largest city in Atlantic Canada, a harbour city overlooked by the star-shaped Citadel fortress and home to Dalhousie University.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab Nova Scotia ak taunit ne oo missing eng' Atlantic Canada, taunit ab bandari ne keerei Citadel (fort ne u kokeliet) ak ole mi Dalhousie University.",
  "Known as the \"City of Bridges\" for the spans across the South Saskatchewan River, and home to the University of Saskatchewan.": "Kigure \"City of Bridges\" amu bridges chechang' che mi barak ab South Saskatchewan River, ak ole mi University of Saskatchewan.",
  "Globally respected degrees": "Degrisiek che kiyan eng' ng'wony tugul",
  "Recognised qualifications across every field of study.": "Sertifiketisiek ak degrisiek che kiyan eng' oratinwek tugul ab somanet.",
  "Choose between career-focused college diplomas and university degrees.": "Lewen eng' diplomasiek ab kolejisiek che indoi chii eng' boisiet ak degrisiek ab univasiti.",
  "Multicultural, high quality of life": "Biik ab ortinwek chechang', sobet ne kararan missing",
  "Welcoming cities that regularly rank among the most liveable in the world.": "Taunisiek che tinye chamyet che kegeer kasarta ak kasarta kou che kararan missing eng' sobet eng' ng'wony.",
  "Research and innovation": "Utafiti ak tuguk che lel",
  "Universities known for research across science, technology and health.": "Univasitisiek che kigen amu utafiti eng' sayansi, teknoloji ak konyoiset.",
  "Engineering & Technology": "Engineering & Technology (Uhandisi ak Teknoloji)",
  "You apply for a study permit with a letter of acceptance from a designated learning institution (DLI) and, for most students, a provincial or territorial attestation letter (PAL). You also need proof that you can pay your tuition and living costs, and a medical exam where required.": "Isomei study permit ak baruet ne mwoe ile kakiyan inyee kong'eten designated learning institution (DLI) ak, eng' kipsomaninik chechang', provincial anan territorial attestation letter (PAL). Imache kora iboru ile imuchi ilipan robinik ab sukul ak robinik ab sobet, ak tiemutik ab kanyoiset ye kimache.",
  "Current study permit fees and financial-proof thresholds are set by Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada and change from time to time.": "Robinik ab study permit che mi raini ak robinik che imache iboru kochobei Immigration, Refugees and Citizenship Canada, ak kowalaksei kasarta ak kasarta.",
