  "High-quality, practical education in a safe, welcoming country.": "Somanet ne kararan ab boisiet ab eunek eng' emet ne tinye kaalyeet ak chamyet.",
  "New Zealand's largest city, known as the \"City of Sails\" and built on a narrow isthmus between two harbours.": "Taunit ne oo missing eng' New Zealand, ne kigure \"City of Sails\" ak ne kichob kobo ng'wony ne ming'in ne mi kwenutab bandarisiek aeng'.",
  "New Zealand's capital and the world's southernmost national capital, known for its compact harbour setting and historic cable car.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab New Zealand ak taunit ne oo ab serikali ne mi kusini missing eng' ng'wony, ne kigen amu bandari nenyin ne ming'in ak cable car ne bo keny.",
  "The largest city in the South Island, known as the \"Garden City\" and home to the University of Canterbury.": "Taunit ne oo missing eng' South Island, ne kigure \"Garden City\" ak ole mi University of Canterbury.",
  "Set on the Waikato River (New Zealand's longest) in a farming region, and home to the University of Waikato.": "Ne mi kobo Waikato River (oinet ne koi missing eng' New Zealand) eng' emet ab mbarenik, ak ole mi University of Waikato.",
  "A coastal Bay of Plenty city beneath Mauao (Mount Maunganui), home to the country's largest port by cargo volume.": "Taunit ab Bay of Plenty ne mi kobo ainet ab nyanjet, ne mi ng'wony ab Mauao (Mount Maunganui), ole mi bandari ne oo missing eng' emet ye kegeer tuguk che keyokte.",
  "A student city with Scottish roots, home to the University of Otago, New Zealand's oldest university, founded in 1869.": "Taunit ab kipsomaninik ne bunu Scotland, ole mi University of Otago, univasiti ne bo keny missing eng' New Zealand, ne kitaun eng' 1869.",
  "Quality-assured education": "Somanet ne kakigimit kararanet nenyin",
  "A national quality framework and a government code of practice set the standard for how providers look after international students.": "Ng'atutik ab serikali ak kerichek ab boisiet kochobei ole ripei sukulisiek kipsomaninik che bunu emotinwek alak.",
  "Practical, hands-on learning": "Somanet ab boisiet ab eunek",
  "Courses that build practical skills, research ability and independent thinking.": "Kosisiek che toretei chii konai boisiet ab eunek, koyai utafiti ak kokabwat eng' tuguk ineendet.",
  "Safe, welcoming communities": "Biik che tinye kaalyeet ak chamyet",
  "Regularly ranked among the most peaceful countries in the world.": "Kegeer kasarta ak kasarta kou agenge eng' emotinwek che tinye kaalyeet missing eng' ng'wony.",
  "Tourism & Hospitality": "Tourism & Hospitality (Utalii ak Ukarimu)",
  "You apply for a Fee Paying Student Visa with an offer of place from an approved education provider, proof that you can pay your tuition fees and living costs, and insurance your provider accepts. You may also be asked for health checks and, for longer stays, police certificates.": "Isomei Fee Paying Student Visa ak ofa ab kaburet kong'eten sukul ne kakiyan, iboru ile imuchi ilipan robinik ab sukul ak robinik ab sobet, ak bima ne yanei sukul neng'ung'. Imuchi kora keteebin health checks ak, ngo ibe kasarta ne koi, police certificates.",
  "Current visa fees and financial-evidence thresholds are set by Immigration New Zealand and change from time to time.": "Robinik ab visa che mi raini ak robinik che imache iboru kochobei Immigration New Zealand, ak kowalaksei kasarta ak kasarta.",
  "Agriculture & Horticulture": "Agriculture & Horticulture (Kilimo ak Kilimo ab Bustani)",
  "The link may be out of date, or the address may have a typo. These are the pages people look for most.": "Imuchi koek link ne bo keny, anan kotinye adres ng'olyon eng' kasiret. Chu ko ukurasaisiek che chengei biik chechang'.",
  "Start from the beginning.": "Taun kong'eten taunet.",
