  "World-renowned universities and a rich academic tradition, with degrees that often take less time than elsewhere.": "Univasitisiek che kigen eng' ng'wony ak somanet ne bo keny, ak degrisiek chechang' che ma nami kasarta ne koi kosiir ole age.",
  "Home to more than 170 museums, many of which offer free admission, including the British Museum.": "Ole mi museums kosiir 170, che chechang' ko ma kelipani si ichut, kobooto British Museum.",
  "Hosts the Edinburgh Festival Fringe, the largest annual arts festival in the world.": "Ole kiyaei Edinburgh Festival Fringe, tuiyet ne oo missing ab sanaa ne kiyaei kenyit age tugul eng' ng'wony.",
  "Scotland's largest city, celebrated for its Victorian and Art Nouveau architecture.": "Taunit ne oo missing eng' Scotland, ne kigen amu korik nenyin ab Victorian ak Art Nouveau.",
  "The UK's second-largest city, with more miles of canal than Venice.": "Taunit ne oo ne bo aeng' eng' UK, ne tinye canals che koi kosiir che mi Venice.",
  "One of the UK's largest financial centres outside London, built on a Victorian textile legacy.": "Agenge eng' taunisiek che echen missing ab rabinik eng' UK ko ma London, ne kichob eng' boisiet ab ngoroik ab kasarta ab Victorian.",
  "Home to the University of Cambridge, founded in 1209 and one of the oldest universities in the world.": "Ole mi University of Cambridge, ne kitaun eng' 1209 ak ne mi agenge eng' univasitisiek che bo keny missing eng' ng'wony.",
  "A major port city on the south coast, from where the RMS Titanic set sail in 1912, and home to the University of Southampton.": "Taunit ne oo ab bandari ne mi kusini, ole ki kobunu RMS Titanic eng' 1912, ak ole mi University of Southampton.",
  "A historic East Anglian city with a Norman cathedral and castle, and England's first UNESCO City of Literature.": "Taunit ne bo keny eng' East Anglia ne tinye cathedral ak castle ab Norman, ak ko England's first UNESCO City of Literature (taunit ne tai eng' England ne kigure kou noton).",
  "A cathedral city on the River Nene in the East of England, with fast rail links to London.": "Taunit ab cathedral ne mi kobo River Nene eng' East of England, ne tinye trains che wendi chokyi agoi London.",
  "The capital of Northern Ireland, where the RMS Titanic was built, now home to the Titanic Belfast visitor experience.": "Taunit ne oo ab serikali ab Northern Ireland, ole ki kichob RMS Titanic, ak raini ole mi Titanic Belfast ne kibunu biik che chomei.",
  "Also known as Derry, a Northern Ireland city whose 17th-century walls are the most complete city walls in Ireland.": "Kigure kora Derry, taunit ab Northern Ireland ne tinye irimeek ab 17th century che bo taunit che kararan missing eng' Ayalandi tugul.",
  "World-renowned universities": "Univasitisiek che kigen eng' ng'wony",
  "Home to some of the world's oldest and most respected universities, offering globally recognised degrees.": "Ole mi univasitisiek alak che bo keny missing ak che kiboiboitu missing eng' ng'wony, che gochei degrisiek che kiyan eng' ng'wony tugul.",
  "A wide choice of courses": "Kosisiek chechang' che imuchi ilewen",
  "Thousands of courses across universities and colleges, from foundation programmes to master's degrees.": "Kosisiek eliphuusyek eng' univasitisiek ak kolejisiek, kong'eten foundation programmes agoi master's degrees.",
  "Shorter degree programmes": "Programisiek ab degrii che ma koi",
  "Many undergraduate degrees run three years and taught master's degrees just one, reducing overall time and cost.": "Degrisiek chechang' ab taunet konamei kenyisiek somok, ak taught master's degrees kenyit agenge kityo, si ma kinam kasarta ne koi ak robinik chechang'.",
  "Rich academic tradition": "Somanet ne bo keny ne kararan",
  "Multicultural cities with centuries of academic history and a huge range of course specialisations.": "Taunisiek ab biik ab ortinwek chechang' che tinye somanet ab kenyisiek pogol chechang', ak kosisiek chechang' missing che terterchin.",
  "Law": "Law (Sheria)",
  "You apply for a Student visa once your university, a licensed student sponsor, gives you a Confirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS). You must show you can pay your course fees and living costs and prove your English, usually at level B2 for a degree. Applicants who live in Kenya also need a tuberculosis (TB) test certificate from an approved clinic.": "Isomei Student visa ye kakogochin univasiti neng'ung', ne tinye licence ab student sponsor, Confirmation of Acceptance for Studies (CAS). Imache iboru ile imuchi ilipan robinik ab kozi ak robinik ab sobet, ak iboru Kiingereza neng'ung', chechang' ko kiwendi ab B2 eng' degrii. Biik che mi Kenya che somei visa komache kora tuberculosis (TB) test certificate kong'eten clinic ne kakiyan.",
  "Current visa fees, financial-evidence thresholds and the Immigration Health Surcharge are set by UK Visas and Immigration and change from time to time.": "Robinik ab visa che mi raini, robinik che imache iboru ak Immigration Health Surcharge kochobei UK Visas and Immigration, ak kowalaksei kasarta ak kasarta.",
